      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `XXHash32Test_verifyChecksum.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/commons-codec/manual/testcases/XXHash32Test/XXHash32Test_verifyChecksum.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test file with better understandability.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. Here's a summary of the understandability improvements made:\n\n1. **Removed mutable instance fields** (`file`, `expectedChecksum`) — they shared state between methods in a confusing way for a parameterized test. Logic is now local to the test method, making the data flow obvious.\n\n2. **Eliminated `initData()`** — the setup helper was an indirection that split initialization from usage. Its logic is now inlined directly in the test method for a clear, linear read.\n\n3. **Better parameter names** — `c` → `expectedChecksum`, `path` → `resourcePath` (clarifying it's a classpath resource, not a filesystem path).\n\n4. **Renamed `toByteArray()`** → `readAllBytes()` — describes intent more precisely.\n\n5. **Removed the `copy()` wrapper** — inlined `IOUtils.copyLarge` directly in `readAllBytes()`, eliminating a layer of indirection.\n\n6. **Named constant** for the magic buffer size `10240` → `COPY_BUFFER_SIZE`.\n\n7. **Formatted `data()` entries** one per line with aligned columns, making it easy to scan the three test cases at a glance."
    }
  ],
  "last_code": "package org.apache.commons.codec.digest;\n\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;\n\nimport java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream;\nimport java.io.FileNotFoundException;\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.io.InputStream;\nimport java.net.URL;\nimport java.nio.file.Files;\nimport java.nio.file.Path;\nimport java.nio.file.Paths;\nimport java.util.stream.Stream;\n\nimport org.apache.commons.io.IOUtils;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.params.ParameterizedTest;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.params.provider.Arguments;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.params.provider.MethodSource;\n\npublic class XXHash32Test_verifyChecksum {\n\n    private static final int COPY_BUFFER_SIZE = 10240;\n\n    // Reference checksums created with xxh32sum: https://cyan4973.github.io/xxHash/\n    static Stream<Arguments> data() {\n        return Stream.of(\n            Arguments.of(\"org/apache/commons/codec/bla.tar\",    \"fbb5c8d1\"),\n            Arguments.of(\"org/apache/commons/codec/bla.tar.xz\", \"4106a208\"),\n            Arguments.of(\"org/apache/commons/codec/small.bin\",  \"f66c26f8\")\n        );\n    }\n\n    private static byte[] readAllBytes(final InputStream input) throws IOException {\n        final ByteArrayOutputStream output = new ByteArrayOutputStream();\n        IOUtils.copyLarge(input, output, new byte[COPY_BUFFER_SIZE]);\n        return output.toByteArray();\n    }\n\n    @ParameterizedTest\n    @MethodSource(\"data\")\n    void verifyChecksum(final String resourcePath, final String expectedChecksum) throws Exception {\n        final URL url = XXHash32Test.class.getClassLoader().getResource(resourcePath);\n        if (url == null) {\n            throw new FileNotFoundException(\"couldn't find \" + resourcePath);\n        }\n        final Path file = Paths.get(url.toURI());\n\n        final XXHash32 hasher = new XXHash32();\n        try (InputStream in = Files.newInputStream(file)) {\n            final byte[] bytes = readAllBytes(in);\n            hasher.update(bytes, 0, bytes.length);\n        }\n\n        assertEquals(expectedChecksum, Long.toHexString(hasher.getValue()), \"checksum for \" + file);\n    }\n}\n",
